Next, create an index route using the `createFileRoute` function.
Because TanStack Router works with file-based routing, every route needs a new file (inside the `app/rooute` directory).
Create the file `app/routes/index.ts` as your first route.
For the purpose of illustration, this route will display a `h1` that says “Hello, World!”:
```
// app/routes/index.tsx
import { createFileRoute } from '@tanstack/react-router';
export const Route = createFileRoute('/')({
component: Home,
});
function Home() {
return <h1>Hello, World!</h1>;
}
```
