# Server Routes | TanStack Start React Docs
created: undefined, last updated: 2026-05-04, [Read more](https://tanstack.com/start/v0/docs/framework/react/guide/server-routes)

Server routes in TanStack Start follow the same file-based routing conventions as TanStack Router.
This means that each file in your routes directory with a server property in the createFileRoute call will be treated as an API route.
...
// routes/hello.ts
import { createFileRoute } from '@tanstack/react-router'
export const Route = createFileRoute('/hello')({
server: {
handlers: {
GET: async ({ request, params }) => {
const user = await findUser(params.id)
if (!user) {
return new Response('User not found', {
status: 404,
})
}
return Response.json(user)
},
},
},
})
